# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# There is deliberately NO `/* /index.html 200` SPA fallback here. That rule is
# what made robots.txt, sitemap.xml, /privacy and /terms all return the app
# shell with HTTP 200 (audit issues P0-02 and P1-10). Every canonical route is
# prerendered to its own HTML file by scripts/prerender.mjs, so Pages serves
# real documents for known paths and 404.html with a 404 status for the rest.

# NOTE ON www CANONICALISATION
#
# There is deliberately no www rule here. A previous revision carried
#   https://www.luggageliason.com/* https://luggageliason.com/:splat 301!
# which never fired, for three separate reasons:
#
#   1. Cloudflare Pages _redirects matches on PATH only. An absolute URL with a
#      scheme and hostname in the source position is not supported, so the rule
#      was inert.
#   2. The trailing "!" force marker is Netlify syntax, not Cloudflare's.
#   3. There is no www DNS record on the zone at all, so nothing ever reaches
#      Pages under that hostname in the first place.
#
# A rule that looks like a canonicalisation policy but does nothing is worse
# than no rule, so it is gone. To actually canonicalise www:
#
#   a. Add a proxied CNAME for www pointing at the Pages project, AND
#   b. add www.luggageliason.com as a custom domain on that project, THEN
#   c. create a Redirect Rule in the dashboard (Rules > Redirect Rules)
#      matching hostname eq "www.luggageliason.com" -> https://luggageliason.com
#      preserving path and query, 301.
#
# See docs/owner-action-checklist.md item 6.
